From de1805afac39794c5362787573be95e0b6a5bf5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:46:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] CI lint: advisory diff steps fetch through
 fetch-merge-base, so git 2.55's promisor BUG no longer skips them

Problem: in lint.yml's Python lints job, "Fetch the merge base" makes the checkout a partial
clone (--filter=tree:0). The two advisory steps after it ("Profile-scope patterns on added
lines", "Public-surface diff vs base") then ran their own `git fetch --deepen=200/1000` on that
clone. On git 2.55.0 a fetch from the promisor remote can die in index-pack:
  BUG: builtin/pack-objects.c:5004: should_include_obj should only be called on existing objects
  fatal: could not finish pack-objects to repack local links
  fatal: index-pack failed   (exit 128)
On 2026-11-13 15:34-16:30Z this hit 11 of ~44 Python-lints jobs, both steps each (22 step
failures; e.g. job 131987878957 of run 43455124649). Both steps are continue-on-error, so the
job stayed green and the two checks silently never ran. PR #2268 (d5c84b2590) gave only
fetch-merge-base.sh a fallback for this BUG.

Five whys:
1. Why did the checks not run? Their first `git fetch --deepen` exited 128 under bash -e.
2. Why 128? git 2.55's index-pack, in promisor mode, aborts while repacking local links.
3. Why promisor mode? Step "Fetch the merge base" had already made the repo a partial clone.
4. Why didn't #2268's fallback catch it? These steps had their own inline fetch, not the script.
5. Why was it invisible? continue-on-error with no annotation: a skipped advisory looks green.

Fix: both steps now fetch the base branch and the PR head commit
(github.event.pull_request.head.sha) with .github/actions/fetch-merge-base/fetch-merge-base.sh,
the same script and fallback as step 1 (one unfiltered retry with the partial-clone config
unset, then restored). It fetches complete commit histories, so the deepen loops are gone. They
pass the head sha as --head (it is the PR head, not the synthetic merge commit, as before). If
the fetch still fails, the step prints one `::warning title=... advisory skipped::` line and
exits 0, so a skipped advisory check is visible and stays advisory. fetch-merge-base.sh is
unchanged.

Test: tests/ci/test_lint_advisory_fetch.py replays both real step scripts from lint.yml on a
partial clone made by the real fetch-merge-base.sh, with a git shim that fails any fetch in
promisor mode (or filtered) with the git 2.55 BUG text and exit 128, and a fake `python` that
records the advisory script's argv and proves a three-dot diff and a blob read on those refs.
- RED on origin/main's lint.yml: 4 failed (both steps exit 128 on the BUG, both steps' "cannot
  succeed" case), 4 passed.
- GREEN: 8 passed; with tests/ci/test_fetch_merge_base.py 18 passed; 9 related CI test files
  (every file naming lint.yml, plus the workflow job graph) 89 passed.
- Mutants, all killed: fallback skipped, fallback still filtered, fallback keeps promisor config,
  config not restored, no ::warning:: line, failed fetch exits 1, wrong --head.
---
